# SLine Admin Rules (when editing sline_admin / admin-ui)

These rules mirror and reference `.agent/rules/`. Enforce them for all Admin Dashboard code.

## Architecture (MVVM)
- **Services** (`*.service.ts`): `'use server'`, `createServiceRoleClient()`, return `ActionResult<T>`, never throw. Only layer that touches the DB.
- **ViewModels** (`use_*.vm.ts`): `'use client'`, state + actions only; `useEffect` only for initial load; never import Supabase/DB.
- **Views** (`*.view.tsx`): Dumb UI only; no `useEffect`, no fetch; data/actions from ViewModel or props.
- Naming: `.model.ts`, `.schema.ts`, `.service.ts`, `.vm.ts`, `.view.tsx`.

## Security
- **Service Role**: Never in client; never in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`; only in Server Actions / server code.
- **Every Server Action**: (1) Zod validate input, (2) verify admin role (e.g. `verifyAdminRole()`), (3) execute, (4) return `{ success, data }` or `{ success: false, error }`.
- **Audit**: Every state-changing call (insert/update/delete) must write to `audit_logs` in the same scope/transaction; include reason for destructive actions.

## UI (Shadcn)
- Use `components/ui/*` (Button, Dialog, Form, etc.). No raw `<button>` when a Shadcn component exists.
- Destructive actions: `variant="destructive"` + confirmation Dialog with mandatory "Reason" for audit.
- Forms: react-hook-form + zod; schema in `models/*.schema.ts`.
- Lists: server-side pagination; no unbounded `select('*')`.

## Never do
- Expose Service Role to client, or put admin actions in client-side Supabase calls.
- Rely on "UI hides the button" for security; always enforce RBAC at server.
- Put business or DB logic in Views or ViewModels.
- Do destructive actions without confirmation, reason, and audit.

For full detail, see `.agent/rules/` and **AGENTS.md**.
